Cell[TextData[{
 "The two ends of that path give the same event: two bindings of a rule are \
one match when they bind the same hyperedges and the rule's left and right \
sides are both unchanged by the exchange of the variables that relates them, \
here ",
 Cell[BoxData["x"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41915581-04ed-47bc-77af-4cebac982d86"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["z"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3329119b-60db-b2d6-62d6-88c5116f003c"],
 ". The canonical hash reads each hyperedge of two vertices in either order. \
Reversing a hyperedge of a path gives a different directed state and the same \
undirected one:"
}], "ExampleText",
 CellID->678322352,ExpressionUUID->"1615cf65-d1a2-5497-3e2a-e74ee0573efd"],

